<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">Democratic Republic of Georgia</h1><p class="st-meta">1918 CE – 1921 CE · capital Tiflis</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Georgia's first modern republic, a Menshevik social democracy that won international recognition before the Red Army invaded in 1921.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>With the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/transcaucasian-democratic-federative-republic">Transcaucasian Democratic Federative Republic</a> collapsing, the Georgian National Council declared independence in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tbilisi">Tiflis</a> on 26 May 1918. German troops arrived to protect the new state against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>, and after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany's</a> defeat British forces took their place until 1920.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Governed by the Social Democratic (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mensheviks">Menshevik</a>) party under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/noe-zhordania">Noe Zhordania</a>, the republic held democratic elections, carried out land reform, founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tbilisi-state-university">Tbilisi State University</a> in 1918 and adopted a constitution in 1921. It fought border wars with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/armenia">Armenia</a> and faced risings in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-ossetia">South Ossetia</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-abkhazia">Abkhazia</a>. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-sfsr">Soviet Russia</a> recognised its independence in the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> of May 1920.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In February 1921 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> invaded, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tbilisi">Tiflis</a> fell on 25 February; the government went into exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/georgian-ssr">Georgian SSR</a> replaced it, and independent <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/georgia">Georgia</a> restored its flag in 1990-1991.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/democratic-republic-of-georgia.jpg" alt="Democratic Republic of Georgia" width="320" height="256"><figcaption>Image: Vector version: Giorgi Balakhadze. Original: Iakob Nikoladze · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Georgia_(1918%E2%80%931921,_4-5).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1918 CE – 1921 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tiflis</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Noe Zhordania, Nikolay Chkheidze</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Georgian Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Georgian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/georgia">Georgia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>First Republic of Georgia, Georgian Democratic Republic</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1920&amp;focus=democratic-republic-of-georgia" aria-label="Democratic Republic of Georgia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5770 691 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Democratic Republic of Georgia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6090 947L6089 946M6090 947L5820 533M6090 947L6091 947"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6089 946h0M5820 533h0M6091 947h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6090 947h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6090 947h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1920&amp;focus=democratic-republic-of-georgia">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
